>> title: Hot Cross Buns
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, bun, easter, currants, spiced
>> counters: Bakery
>> servings: 12
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: narrow — this dough proofs faster than it looks, and buns pushed past the second proof bake flat-topped and pull apart at the joins

>> step: stir, stand 10 min
Stir @warm whole milk{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL) with @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let stand ~{10%min}.

>> step: add and knead 8 min
Add @bread flour{3 3/4%cup}(500 g), @mixed spice{2%tsp}(5 g; cinnamon, nutmeg, and allspice), @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g), @egg{1%large}, and @softened unsalted butter{5%Tbs}(70 g) to @&(~1)yeast mixture{}, then knead ~{8%min}.

>> step: knead in the fruit, rise until doubled
Knead @currants{1%cup}(150 g) and @orange zest{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)dough{}, then rise until doubled, ~{1 1/2%hours}.

>> step: divide into 12 buns in a 9x13-in pan, proof 45 min
Divide @&(~1)dough{} into 12 buns in a #9x13-in pan{} and proof ~{45%min}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(60 g), @water{5%Tbs}(75 mL) to a smooth paste.

>> step: pipe the crosses, bake 375°F 22 min
Pipe crosses of @&(~1)flour paste{} onto @&(~2)buns{} and bake at 375°F for ~{22%min}.

>> step: brush with warm jam
Brush @&(~1)buns{} with warmed @apricot jam{2%Tbs}(40 g).
